# Fathom — Art assets

Fathom's art is supplied with the project, under `assets/`. Seven sprite sheets cover
the forager, the three predators, the bonus drifter, the flare bloom, and the maze
tiles, and the build renders each of those elements from its sheet. Everything else
the game shows is drawn in code, and the last section of this file lists it.

## How the sheets are organized

Each sheet is a folder under `assets/` holding one PNG per frame, named by its frame
index (`0.png`, `1.png`, and so on). Every PNG has a transparent background in
straight alpha, so only its drawn pixels are opaque and each frame composites cleanly
over the dark maze.

| Sheet | Folder | Frames | Frame size | What it covers |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Forager | `assets/glimmerfin/` | 8 (`0`–`7`) | 32 x 32 | The player character |
| Lanternjaw | `assets/lanternjaw/` | 16 (`0`–`15`) | 32 x 32 | The light-seeking predator, both of its forms |
| Gloamfin | `assets/gloamfin/` | 8 (`0`–`7`) | 32 x 32 | The sound-seeking predator |
| Flarefish | `assets/flarefish/` | 8 (`0`–`7`) | 32 x 32 | The flare-making predator |
| Bonus drifter | `assets/drifter/` | 8 (`0`–`7`) | 32 x 32 | The harmless amber jellyfish |
| Flare bloom | `assets/flare-bloom/` | 8 (`0`–`7`) | 128 x 128 | The Flarefish's radial flare |
| Maze tiles | `assets/trench-walls/` | 19 (`0`–`18`) | 32 x 32 | Wall autotile, floor, fog, den gate |

Frame sizes are in pixels of source art. A tile is `TILE` (`32`) logical units square,
so a 32 x 32 frame maps onto one tile at a scale of one.

## How they are drawn

- A 32 x 32 frame is drawn over one tile at its subject's position. A creature frame
  carries a margin inside its box, so the creature reads as centered on its tile; a
  maze tile fills its cell edge to edge and butts seamlessly against its neighbors.
- The sprites and tiles are pixel art, and they stay crisp at every scale the stage is
  fitted to.
- The flare bloom is an area effect far larger than a tile. It is drawn centered on the
  Flarefish and scaled so its lit radius matches the flare radius
  `specs/predators/flarefish.md` fixes, and it reads as light over the maze rather than
  as an opaque disc.

## How they are loaded

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build loads the frames itself. Every URL it requests resolves against the page
rather than against the origin root, so the produced site runs unchanged whether it is
served from the root of a static host or mounted under a sub-path. The produced site
is self-contained and carries every frame it draws.
{{else}}
The {{engine.name}} engine provides the asset loader, documented in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. It resolves every path under one root,
`assets/`, relative to the page the build is served from, and it fetches and decodes
the file. The build loads each frame through that loader rather than requesting a URL
of its own, writing the path relative to that root: `glimmerfin/0.png`,
`trench-walls/16.png`.

The produced site serves every seeded frame under that root, so a path the loader
resolves reaches the seeded file at whatever base path the site is served from.
{{/if}}

## The forager: `assets/glimmerfin/`

Eight frames, a two-frame chomp pair for each of the four facings.

| Frames | Facing | First frame | Second frame |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0, 1 | down | mouth closed | mouth open |
| 2, 3 | up | mouth closed | mouth open |
| 4, 5 | left | mouth closed | mouth open |
| 6, 7 | right | mouth closed | mouth open |

Alternate the pair for the forager's current facing while it travels, at about 8 to 10
frames per second, and hold the mouth-closed frame while it is at rest.

The sheet carries no glow. The forager's brightness and its lit pocket are runtime
light drawn around the sprite, listed at the end of this file. A lives icon in the HUD
may reuse a forager frame.

## The Lanternjaw: `assets/lanternjaw/`

Sixteen frames in two forms. Frames 0 to 7 are its true anglerfish body, a two-frame
pair per facing: an amber bell above dark, gaping jaws. Frames 8 to 15 are the
jellyfish disguise, an eight-frame tendril-sway loop that is the same art as
`assets/drifter/` frames 0 to 7, pixel for pixel.

| Frames | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| 0, 1 | True body, facing down |
| 2, 3 | True body, facing up |
| 4, 5 | True body, facing left |
| 6, 7 | True body, facing right |
| 8–15 | The jellyfish disguise, one eight-frame sway loop |

The amber bell sits in the same place and is drawn the same in both forms, so the two
differ only in what hangs beneath it: the drifter's tendrils, or the hunter's jaws.

- In `"chase"`, draw the pair for its facing from frames 0 to 7 and alternate them at
  about 6 to 8 frames per second, so its jaws show beneath the bell.
- In `"wander"`, play frames 8 to 15 as a loop at about 8 frames per second, animated
  exactly as the bonus drifter is, so a wandering Lanternjaw reads as a drifter up
  close.
- Its body is drawn only where it is lit. The amber bulb-light that shows it in the
  dark at any distance is drawn in code and listed at the end of this file.

