## The bonus drifter: `assets/drifter/`

Eight frames: an amber bell with a frilled skirt and a few tendrils below it, over one
sway loop. A jellyfish reads the same whichever way it drifts, so the sheet is one loop
rather than per-facing pairs. Advance the loop at about 8 frames per second while it
moves.

These are the frames a wandering Lanternjaw wears as its disguise, and the bell here is
the bell baked into the Lanternjaw's true-body frames. Like a predator body, the
jellyfish is drawn only where the drifter is lit, so in the dark a drifter shows as its
amber bulb-light alone and its tendrils appear only up close. `specs/sensing.md` fixes
what a sonar pulse reveals.

## The flare bloom: `assets/flare-bloom/`

Eight frames at 128 x 128, a warm radial burst in three beats. The frames are already
warm-colored and are composited with no tint.

| Frames | Beat | Played over |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0, 1, 2 | Charge-up: a small warm glow swelling toward a white core | The pre-bloom charge-up |
| 3, 4, 5 | Bloom: a white-hot core ringed by warm light, widest and brightest at frame 5 | The bloom |
| 6, 7 | Fade: the bloom collapses and dims | Drawn after the bloom ends, while the flare is already over |

`specs/predators/flarefish.md` fixes how long each beat lasts and how large the lit
disc is. Frame 5 is scaled so its lit radius is that flare radius.

## The maze tiles: `assets/trench-walls/`

Nineteen frames: a sixteen-frame wall autotile (`0`–`15`), the corridor floor (`16`),
the unrevealed fog tile (`17`), and the den gate (`18`). Each fills its 32 x 32 cell
edge to edge with no margin.

### The wall autotile

A wall tile's frame index is the sum of one bit for each of its four orthogonal
neighbors that is also a wall tile.

| Side | Bit |
| --- | --- |
| N (up) | 1 |
| E (right) | 2 |
| S (down) | 4 |
| W (left) | 8 |

A connected side runs flush to that edge and merges with its neighbor. A side with no
wall neighbor faces a corridor and carries a rounded raised rock face with a rim light
along it.

| Frame | Connected sides | Piece |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | none | Isolated pillar |
| 1 | N | Bottom end of a vertical wall |
| 2 | E | Left end of a horizontal wall |
| 3 | N, E | Elbow |
| 4 | S | Top end of a vertical wall |
| 5 | N, S | Vertical straight |
| 6 | E, S | Elbow |
| 7 | N, E, S | T-junction, open left |
| 8 | W | Right end of a horizontal wall |
| 9 | N, W | Elbow |
| 10 | E, W | Horizontal straight |
| 11 | N, E, W | T-junction, open down |
| 12 | S, W | Elbow |
| 13 | N, S, W | T-junction, open right |
| 14 | E, S, W | T-junction, open up |
| 15 | all four | Fully enclosed interior |

### The floor, the fog, and the gate

| Frame | Tile | Drawn |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 16 | Corridor floor, seamless when repeated | Under everything else, on every open tile |
| 17 | Unrevealed ground: flat, featureless, and darker than the floor | On every tile still unrevealed |
| 18 | Den gate: a floor tile crossed by a barred threshold | On the single gate tile of the den chamber |

Visibility is shading over these same tiles rather than separate frames. A lit tile is
the tile at full brightness, a remembered tile is the same wall or floor tile drawn
dim, and an unrevealed tile reads as the value of frame 17. `specs/sensing.md` fixes
when a tile is in each state. Predators, the drifter, the plankton, and the effects are
layered over the tiles.

## What is drawn in code

No sheet covers the following. Each is rendered by the build, and the spec named
beside it fixes its behavior and its appearance.

| Drawn in code | Fixed by |
| --- | --- |
| The plankton motes | `specs/gameplay.md` |
| The sonar wavefront, for the forager's pulse and the Gloamfin's pings alike | `specs/sensing.md`, `specs/predators/gloamfin.md` |
| The amber bulb-light, drawn identically for the bonus drifter and the Lanternjaw so the two read alike at a distance | `specs/sensing.md`, `specs/gameplay.md`, `specs/predators.md` |
| The detection alert flash a predator fires the instant it takes a fix | `specs/predators.md` |
| The ink cloud | `specs/sensing.md` |
| The forager's brightness glow and its lit pocket, and the shading that draws a lit, remembered, or unrevealed tile | `specs/sensing.md` |
| The HUD, every screen, menu, panel, and overlay, and all text | `specs/ui.md` |
